    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- Update the `predict` function. Given a `token`, it should return a list of up to five tokens. Each token in the list should be a random follower of the token before it.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRecall you can use a `for` loop to iterate five times.\r\n\r\n```\r\nfor i in range(5):\r\n  ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nConsider still checking if a token is in `model` before retrieving its follower. But this time, if a token isn’t in `model`, just stop early.\r\n\r\n```\r\nif token in model:\r\n  # Add to list of followers\r\nelse:\r\n  break\r\n```",
